{"id":"0d076e8d609b49f03e54f24a89cce360ac0237f0","axis":"silent","repo":"apache/cxf","sha":"0d076e8d609b49f03e54f24a89cce360ac0237f0","parsed":{"files":[{"path":"distribution/src/main/release/release_notes.txt","lines":["@@ -33,6 +33,17 @@ Important notes:","   must return a fresh stream positioned at the beginning. Persistence and","   retransmission may read the original attachment more than once, including","   when WS-Security signs or encrypts attachments.","+* HTTP Signature: when an inbound request or response signs the \"Date\" header,","+  MessageVerifier now rejects it if the Date is more than 300 seconds old or","+  more than 60 seconds in the future. Deployments that sign \"Date\" with more","+  clock skew than this, or send fixed dates, will start failing. The limits can","+  be changed with \"rs.security.http.signature.time.to.live\" and","+  \"rs.security.http.signature.future.time.to.live\" (or the MessageVerifier","+  setters). A time to live of 0 or less disables the age check, a future time to","+  live of 0 allows no clock skew and a negative value disables the future check.","+  The check only gives replay protection when \"date\" is signed and listed in","+  \"rs.security.http.signature.in.headers\", and a message can still be replayed","+  within the time window."," "," Users are encouraged to review the migration guide at:"," https://cxf.apache.org/docs/42-migration-guide.html"],"additions":11,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"rt/rs/security/http-signature/src/main/java/org/apache/cxf/rs/security/httpsignature/HTTPSignatureConstants.java","lines":["@@ -52,6 +52,29 @@ public final class HTTPSignatureConstants extends RSSecurityConstants {","      */","     public static final String RSSEC_HTTP_SIGNATURE_DIGEST_ALGORITHM = \"rs.security.http.signature.digest.algorithm\";"," ","+    /**","+     * The maximum age in seconds of a signed \"Date\" header on an inbound request or response. A message whose","+     * signed \"Date\" is older than this is rejected, so that a captured signed message can not be replayed","+     * after its time to live has passed. The default is 300 seconds, a value of 0 or less disables the check.","+     * A value set directly on the MessageVerifier takes precedence.","+     *","+     * The check only applies when the sender signs the \"Date\" header, which CreateSignatureInterceptor does not","+     * add by default. To get replay protection, the sender must sign \"date\" and the receiver must also add","+     * \"date\" to \"rs.security.http.signature.in.headers\" so that messages without a signed \"Date\" are rejected.","+     * There is no nonce or replay cache, so a message can still be replayed within the time to live.","+     */","+    public static final String RSSEC_HTTP_SIGNATURE_TIME_TO_LIVE = \"rs.security.http.signature.time.to.live\";","+","+    /**","+     * The number of seconds a signed \"Date\" header on an inbound request or response may be in the future,","+     * to allow for clock skew. The default is 60 seconds, a value of 0 allows no clock skew and a negative value","+     * disables the check. With the check disabled, a message with a signed \"Date\" in the future stays within the","+     * time to live until that date. A value set directly on the MessageVerifier takes precedence. See","+     * RSSEC_HTTP_SIGNATURE_TIME_TO_LIVE for the limits of this check.","+     */","+    public static final String RSSEC_HTTP_SIGNATURE_FUTURE_TIME_TO_LIVE =","+        \"rs.security.http.signature.future.time.to.live\";","+"," ","     private HTTPSignatureConstants() {","         // complete"],"additions":23,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"rt/rs/security/http-signature/src/main/java/org/apache/cxf/rs/security/httpsignature/MessageVerifier.java","lines":["@@ -18,17 +18,21 @@","  */"," package org.apache.cxf.rs.security.httpsignature;"," ","+import java.text.ParseException;"," import java.util.ArrayList;"," import java.util.Collections;"," import java.util.List;"," import java.util.Map;"," import java.util.Objects;","+import java.util.concurrent.TimeUnit;"," import java.util.logging.Logger;"," "," import org.apache.cxf.common.logging.LogUtils;"," import org.apache.cxf.helpers.CastUtils;","+import org.apache.cxf.jaxrs.utils.HttpUtils;"," import org.apache.cxf.message.Message;"," import org.apache.cxf.message.MessageUtils;","+import org.apache.cxf.rs.security.httpsignature.exception.InvalidSignatureException;"," import org.apache.cxf.rs.security.httpsignature.exception.MissingSignatureHeaderException;"," import org.apache.cxf.rs.security.httpsignature.exception.MultipleSignatureHeaderException;"," import org.apache.cxf.rs.security.httpsignature.provider.AlgorithmProvider;","@@ -36,8 +40,18 @@"," import org.apache.cxf.rs.security.httpsignature.provider.SecurityProvider;"," import org.apache.cxf.rs.security.httpsignature.utils.DefaultSignatureConstants;"," import org.apache.cxf.rs.security.httpsignature.utils.SignatureHeaderUtils;","+import org.tomitribe.auth.signatures.Signature;"," "," public class MessageVerifier {","+    /**","+     * The default maximum age in seconds of a signed \"Date\" header","+     */","+    public static final int DEFAULT_TIME_TO_LIVE = 300;","+    /**","+     * The default number of seconds a signed \"Date\" header may be in the future","+     */","+    public static final int DEFAULT_FUTURE_TIME_TO_LIVE = 60;","+","     private static final Logger LOG = LogUtils.getL7dLogger(MessageVerifier.class);"," ","     private AlgorithmProvider algorithmProvider;","@@ -46,6 +60,8 @@ public class MessageVerifier {","     private final SignatureValidator signatureValidator;","     private final List<String> requiredHeaders;","     private boolean addDefaultRequiredHeaders = true;","+    private Integer timeToLive;","+    private Integer futureTimeToLive;"," ","     public MessageVerifier(KeyProvider keyProvider) {","         this(keyProvider, (List<String>)null);","@@ -151,9 +167,74 @@ public void verifyMessage(Map<String, List<String>> messageHeaders, String metho","                                     method,","                                     uri,","                                     signedHeaders);","+        verifyDateHeader(messageHeaders, m);","         LOG.fine(\"Finished signature verification\");","     }"," ","+    /**","+     * Reject a message whose signed \"Date\" header is outside the configured time window, so that a captured","+     * signed message can not be replayed once its time to live has passed. A \"Date\" header which is not","+     * covered by the signature is ignored, as it can be changed along with the rest of the unsigned message.","+     * Values set on this class take precedence over the contextual properties.","+     */","+    private void verifyDateHeader(Map<String, List<String>> messageHeaders, Message m) {","+        int ttl = timeToLive != null ? timeToLive","+            : getContextualInteger(m, HTTPSignatureConstants.RSSEC_HTTP_SIGNATURE_TIME_TO_LIVE, DEFAULT_TIME_TO_LIVE);","+        int futureTtl = futureTimeToLive != null ? futureTimeToLive","+            : getContextualInteger(m, HTTPSignatureConstants.RSSEC_HTTP_SIGNATURE_FUTURE_TIME_TO_LIVE,","+                                   DEFAULT_FUTURE_TIME_TO_LIVE);","+        // A time to live of 0 would reject every message, so 0 or less disables the age check. For the future","+        // check 0 means no clock skew is allowed and only a negative value disables it.","+        if (ttl <= 0 && futureTtl < 0) {","+            return;","+        }","+        List<String> signedHeaders = Signature.fromString(messageHeaders.get(\"Signature\").get(0)).getHeaders();","+        if (!signedHeaders.contains(\"date\")) {","+            return;","+        }","+        // Check the same value that was signed, see SignatureHeaderUtils.mapHeaders","+        List<String> dates = new ArrayList<>();","+        for (Map.Entry<String, List<String>> entry : messageHeaders.entrySet()) {","+            if (\"date\".equalsIgnoreCase(entry.getKey())) {","+                dates.addAll(entry.getValue());","+            }","+        }","+        if (dates.isEmpty()) {","+            return;","+        }","+        if (dates.size() > 1) {","+            throw new InvalidSignatureException(\"there are multiple signed Date header values\");","+        }","+        final long dateTime;","+        try {","+            dateTime = HttpUtils.getHttpDateFormat().parse(dates.get(0)).getTime();","+        } catch (ParseException ex) {","+            throw new InvalidSignatureException(\"the signed Date header can not be parsed\");","+        }","+        long now = System.currentTimeMillis();","+        if (ttl > 0 && now - dateTime > TimeUnit.SECONDS.toMillis(ttl)) {","+            throw new InvalidSignatureException(\"the signed Date header is older than the time to live\");","+        }","+        if (futureTtl >= 0 && dateTime - now > TimeUnit.SECONDS.toMillis(futureTtl)) {","+            throw new InvalidSignatureException(\"the signed Date header is in the future\");","+        }","+    }","+","+    private static int getContextualInteger(Message m, String key, int defaultValue) {","+        Object value = m.getContextualProperty(key);","+        if (value instanceof Number) {","+            return ((Number)value).intValue();","+        }","+        if (value instanceof String) {","+            try {","+                return Integer.parseInt((String)value);","+            } catch (NumberFormatException ex) {","+                LOG.warning(\"Incorrect integer value of \" + value + \" specified for: \" + key);","+            }","+        }","+        return defaultValue;","+    }","+","     private void inspectMultipleSignatureHeaders(Map<String, List<String>> responseHeaders) {","         if (responseHeaders.get(\"Signature\").size() > 1) {","             throw new MultipleSignatureHeaderException(\"there are multiple signature headers in request\");","@@ -178,4 +259,41 @@ public void setAddDefaultRequiredHeaders(boolean addDefaultRequiredHeaders) {","         this.addDefaultRequiredHeaders = addDefaultRequiredHeaders;","     }"," ","+    /**","+     * Return the configured maximum age in seconds of a signed \"Date\" header, or null if it was not set on","+     * this class, in which case the contextual property or the default of 300 seconds is used.","+     */","+    public Integer getTimeToLive() {","+        return timeToLive;","+    }","+","+    /**","+     * Set the maximum age in seconds of a signed \"Date\" header. A message whose signed \"Date\" is older","+     * than this is rejected. This takes precedence over the \"rs.security.http.signature.time.to.live\"","+     * contextual property. The default is 300 seconds, a value of 0 or less disables the check, and null","+     * falls back to the contextual property.","+     */","+    public void setTimeToLive(Integer timeToLive) {","+        this.timeToLive = timeToLive;","+    }","+","+    /**","+     * Return the configured number of seconds a signed \"Date\" header may be in the future, or null if it was","+     * not set on this class, in which case the contextual property or the default of 60 seconds is used.","+     */","+    public Integer getFutureTimeToLive() {","+        return futureTimeToLive;","+    }","+","+    /**","+     * Set the number of seconds a signed \"Date\" header may be in the future, to allow for clock skew.","+     * This takes precedence over the \"rs.security.http.signature.future.time.to.live\" contextual property.","+     * The default is 60 seconds, a value of 0 allows no clock skew, a negative value disables the check, and","+     * null falls back to the contextual property. With the check disabled, a message with a signed \"Date\" in","+     * the future stays within the time to live until that date.","+     */","+    public void setFutureTimeToLive(Integer futureTimeToLive) {","+        this.futureTimeToLive = futureTimeToLive;","+    }","+"," }"],"additions":118,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"rt/rs/security/http-signature/src/main/java/org/apache/cxf/rs/security/httpsignature/utils/SignatureHeaderUtils.java","lines":["@@ -21,9 +21,8 @@"," import java.net.URI;"," import java.security.MessageDigest;"," import java.security.NoSuchAlgorithmException;","-import java.time.Clock;","-import java.time.LocalDateTime;"," import java.time.ZoneOffset;","+import java.time.ZonedDateTime;"," import java.time.format.DateTimeFormatter;"," import java.util.Base64;"," import java.util.Collections;","@@ -42,8 +41,7 @@ private SignatureHeaderUtils() { }","      * Add a date header at the current time using the ZoneOffset. Date format is http","      */","     public static void addDateHeader(Map<String, List<String>> messageHeaders, ZoneOffset zoneOffset) {","-        String date = DateTimeFormatter.RFC_1123_DATE_TIME","-                .format(LocalDateTime.now().atZone(Clock.system(zoneOffset).getZone()));","+        String date = DateTimeFormatter.RFC_1123_DATE_TIME.format(ZonedDateTime.now(zoneOffset));","         messageHeaders.put(\"Date\", Collections.singletonList(date));","     }"," "],"additions":2,"deletions":4,"truncated":false},{"path":"rt/rs/security/http-signature/src/test/java/org/apache/cxf/rs/security/httpsignature/MessageVerifierTest.java","lines":["@@ -18,12 +18,17 @@","  */"," package org.apache.cxf.rs.security.httpsignature;"," ","+import java.beans.Introspector;","+import java.beans.PropertyDescriptor;"," import java.io.IOException;"," import java.security.KeyPair;"," import java.security.KeyPairGenerator;"," import java.security.NoSuchAlgorithmException;"," import java.time.ZoneOffset;","+import java.time.ZonedDateTime;","+import java.time.format.DateTimeFormatter;"," import java.util.ArrayList;","+import java.util.Arrays;"," import java.util.Collections;"," import java.util.HashMap;"," import java.util.List;","@@ -32,6 +37,7 @@"," import javax.crypto.KeyGenerator;"," import